<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/7th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Degsastan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">603</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Degsastan was fought in 603 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aethelfrith-of-northumbria">Æthelfrith of Bernicia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aedan-mac-gabrain">Áedán mac Gabráin</a>, king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dal-riata">Dál Riata</a>, who led a large army including Irish allies. Æthelfrith won decisively despite heavy losses, including his brother Theodbald, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bede">Bede</a> wrote that no king of the Scots dared fight the English again until his own day. The site is uncertain, perhaps Dawston in Liddesdale.</p></div>
